{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_53","type":"agent_message","text":"The fused transpose-add is a clear win once enough GPU work exists ahead of it, but its Python launch cost hurts batch-1 cases; I’m gating it accordingly. More importantly, folding normalization directly into a channel-tiled GRN kernel is still bitwise exact and saves an additional 5–10 μs, including the previously slow tiny 7×7 cases."}}
